    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0474" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.652/119: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-20T14:00:00-05:00">November 20, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. Your 481, November 19, noon.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d342-f1"/> From Sayre. I
                    suggest if you see no objection that you inform the Italian Government that we
                    are now at work on a reply but that if, as seems likely, the new treaty is not
                    signed by December 15 we hope to bridge the interval before the new treaty comes
                    into force by working out some arrangement covering the generalizing of trade
                    agreement rates to Italian products. Personal letter follows giving further
                        particulars.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d342-f2"/> [Sayre.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
